            <title>[LU-21020] Read of a mirrored file fails with EIO during an OST failover</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21020</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;While the OSTs of a mirrored file are unavailable (an OSS failover, a dead OSS, also the MDT for the DoM component), reads of the file fail with EIO, either within milliseconds or after one RPC timeout. Reads of a file with one mirror wait for the targets and succeed. On a test cluster, a 120 s outage gave thousands of EIO on mirrored files and none on files with one mirror.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Reproducer"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproducer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two OSTs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-bash"&gt;
lfs setstripe -N -Eeof -o0 -N -Eeof -o1 f
dd &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/urandom of=f bs=1M count=4; lfs mirror resync f
dd &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/urandom of=f bs=4k count=1 seek=10 conv=notrunc    &lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;# one mirror stale
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;# stop both OSTs, wait &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;until&lt;/span&gt; the client's OSC imports are no longer FULL, &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;cat f &amp;gt; /dev/null    &lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;# Input/output error at once, not waiting &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; the OSTs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A read is non-delay. When the OSC import is not healthy it fails with &lt;tt&gt;-EAGAIN&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;cl_io_loop()&lt;/tt&gt; restarts it on the next mirror. After four rounds over the mirrors &lt;tt&gt;lov_io_mirror_init()&lt;/tt&gt; sets &lt;tt&gt;ci_tried_all_mirrors&lt;/tt&gt; to stop the fast switching, but &lt;tt&gt;ci_ndelay&lt;/tt&gt; stays set: the lock enqueue (&lt;tt&gt;LDLM_FL_NDELAY&lt;/tt&gt;) and the BRW (&lt;tt&gt;rq_no_delay&lt;/tt&gt;) fail at once with &lt;tt&gt;-EAGAIN&lt;/tt&gt;, which &lt;tt&gt;cl_io_loop()&lt;/tt&gt; turns into &lt;tt&gt;-EIO&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do not set &lt;tt&gt;LDLM_FL_NDELAY&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;OBD_BRW_NDELAY&lt;/tt&gt; once &lt;tt&gt;ci_tried_all_mirrors&lt;/tt&gt; is set, so that try waits for its mirror like a read of a file with one mirror. It waits for that mirror only, until its target is back or the client is evicted. New &lt;tt&gt;sanity-flr&lt;/tt&gt; test 33d. Patch to follow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12669" title="FLR-EC: recover data from parity code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12669"&gt;LU-12669&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17973" title="FLR2: improve read mirror selection for many copies" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17973"&gt;LU-17973&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
